'''Warlmanpa''' (also '''Walmala''') is a nearly [[language extinction|extinct]] [[Australian Aboriginal languages|Australian Aboriginal language]] spoken by the [[Warlmanpa]] people.

The [[Warlmanpa]] have a highly developed [[Warlmanpa Sign Language|sign language]].

One of the first recordings of this language was made by [[Kenneth L. Hale|Kenneth Hale]] in his interview with [[Donald Jupurrula Graham]] in 1966.<ref name=":0">{{Cite book |last1=Nash |first1=David |url=https://hdl.handle.net/10070/492231 |title=Northern Territory Dictionary of Biography |publisher=Charles Darwin University Press |year=2008 |isbn=9780980457810 |edition=Rev |location=Darwin |pages=233 |chapter=Donald Jupurrula Graham (c1920-1989) |hdl=10070/492231 |access-date=2025-06-24}}{{dead link|date=April 2025}}</ref>

